-- title:
--   L² approximation of slab profiles by Paley–Wiener profiles
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field and let $\alpha\colon (\mathbb{A}_F)^\times \to \mathbb{R}^\times$ be the unit-group homomorphism induced by the distributive Haar character of the adele ring; assume $\alpha(x)>0$ for all $x$. Fix reals $0<d_1<d_2$, a set $\Phi$ of points of $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ (serving as the fundamental-domain field of the carrier pins `productionPinsOf`, whose central subgroup $Z$ is the whole idele group), a continuous unitary character $\xi$ of that $Z$, and a function $\varphi\colon GL_2(\mathbb{A}_F)\to\mathbb{C}$ which is a slab profile for $\xi$: measurable, left invariant under adelic unipotent matrices and under global Borel points, transforming by $\xi$ under central scalars, bounded on each determinant slab, and vanishing off a height band. Fix $a,b$ with $0<a$ such that $\varphi(g)\neq 0$ forces $\mathrm{adelicHeight}_F(g)\in[a,b]$. Assume further: a measure $\rho$ on a measurable space $T$, a map $\mathrm{ev}\colon T\to GL_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ and $\kappa\neq\infty$ with $\|\varphi-\psi\|_{L^2}$ over the quotient of $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ by the subgroup generated by the rational torus and the adelic unipotent group, restricted to the slab where the idele norm of the determinant lies in $[d_1,d_2]$ and computed along chosen representatives, bounded by $\kappa\|\varphi\circ\mathrm{ev}-\psi\circ\mathrm{ev}\|_{L^2(T,\rho)}$ for every slab profile $\psi$ for $\xi$; a set $E$ of functions on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ such that each finite sum $\sum_i e_i$ of members of $E$ is realised as the profile of a Paley–Wiener datum, namely a finite index set $\iota$, characters $\mu_e,\nu_e$ of the ideles that are unitary, trivial on principal ideles and continuous, with $\mu_e\nu_e=\xi$ on $Z$, a swap $r$ interchanging $\mu$ and $\nu$, pairwise separation of the indices by some norm-one idele, and a family $\psi_f(e,s)$ of sections induced from $\mu_e\alpha^{s+1/2}$ and $\nu_e\alpha^{-(s+1/2)}$ along the adelic Borel subgroup, jointly continuous, entire in $s$, $K_\infty$-finite and $K_f$-smooth, with finite-dimensional right translates under the archimedean row-isometry subgroup at each infinite place and uniform integrable bounds $(1+|t|)^n\|\psi_f(e,\sigma'+it,g)\|\le m(t)$ on vertical strips over compacta, such that $\psi$ is a slab profile for $\xi$, equals $\sum_e (4\pi)^{-1}\int_{\mathbb{R}}\psi_f(e,\sigma'+it,\cdot)\,dt$ for every abscissa $\sigma'$, is supported in the band $[a,b]$, and equals $\sum_i e_i$; and density: for every $\delta>0$ some finite sum of members of $E$ approximates $\varphi$ within $\delta$ in $L^2(T,\rho)$ after composing with $\mathrm{ev}$. The conclusion asserts the existence of $a'>0$ and $b'$ with $\varphi$ supported in the height band $[a',b']$ such that for every $\varepsilon>0$ there is a Paley–Wiener datum with all the properties just listed, with band $[a',b']$ in place of $[a,b]$ and with the $L^2$ distance from $\varphi$ on the slab-restricted quotient less than $\varepsilon$.
--
--   This is the assembly step in the proof that Paley–Wiener slab profiles are dense, with its three analytic inputs — the comparison between the quotient norm and the norm on $(T,\rho)$, the realisability of finite elementary sums as Paley–Wiener profiles, and the density of such sums — taken as hypotheses. It is used by [`AutomorphicForm.exists_isSlabProfile_paleyWiener_eLpNorm_sub_restrict_rationalTorusUnipotentQuotient_lt_of_isSlabProfile`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_isSlabProfile_paleyWiener_eLpNorm_sub_restrict_rationalTorusUnipotentQuotient_lt_of_isSlabProfile), where these hypotheses are discharged for an explicit choice of $T$, $\mathrm{ev}$ and $\rho$.
